# Vibe theory's mathematics, machine-checked. The substrate is a hyperbolic mesh of docks, each dock 24 slots of one
# tone each, updated by one reversible integer rule. Every structure that description names is modeled in code/vibe
# and proved to have the properties the theory uses:
#
#   law          the law kit: one template per algebraic or dynamical law, one line per law at each structure
#   tone         the tone is the field F3; charge conjugation is negation; balanced ternary adds exactly
#   lean         the order fear < calm < love, reversed by conjugation, not compatible with the residue sum
#   eisenstein   Z[w]: ring laws, w^3 = 1, the norm, reduction to F3, the primes 2, 3, 7, the units
#   coin         the coin and the meeting: exact unitarity, eigenvalues, determinant w, the top speed 1/2
#   role         the qutrit phase space Z3 x Z3, its symplectic form, the 12 stabilizer lines of AG(2, 3)
#   heisenberg   the 27 Weyl operators: group laws, Z X = w X Z, exponent 3, the center
#   hurwitz      2T = Q8 x| Z3, the 24 Hurwitz units, checked against the quaternions
#   turn         SL(2, 3) is 2T, by an explicit isomorphism; the Clifford action on the Weyl operators
#   dock         the 24 slots as tetrads: lines, frames, W(D4), W(F4), triality, and the slots ARE the units
#   design       the slots are a spherical 5-design and not a 6-design; the husk's moments
#   honeycomb    Gram determinants: {3,4,3} spherical, {4,3,4} flat, {3,4,3,4} hyperbolic
#   warp         the cone-type matrix, its cubic, the shells, the warp factor in (18.278, 18.279)
#   growth       Margenstern's Fibonacci splitting of {7,3}
#   forced-dock-24-cell   the shells (1 + 2x)^4 of the tetrads, the 24-cell as the two-vibe shell
#   knit         the contact (bounce and pass), the store, the earliest pair map: reversible and conserving
#   line         a ring of docks under the knit: the line law, reversibility, C and time reversal, motion at speed 1
#   mesh         the D4 lattice as the mesh's flat stand-in
#   clifford     Cl(4) on blades; the volume element and the split of Cl+(4)
#   boost        velocity addition as hyperbolic numbers; the interval, light stays light
#   hopf         the dock's Hopf fibration: six circles of four over an octahedron
#   beat, wake   time as a count with its one-way order; the mesh's one-way growth
#   site         the four sign choices of a slot within its pair of axes, paired by the opposite
#
# The theorems below hold across modules, so they check that the layers agree with each other: the frame a slot sits
# in (read off its coordinates in vibe/dock) is the axis its Hopf circle lies over (read off the group in vibe/hopf),
# and the full turn -1 of the dock is the opposite slot and the matrix -I of the grid.

load @term/seed/vibe/tone
  find tone

load @term/seed/vibe/hurwitz
  find hurwitz-element
  find hurwitz-core
  find q8-axis
  find minus-one-unit
  find hurwitz-product

load @term/seed/vibe/dock
  find unit-slot
  find frame-of
  find opposite
  find same-tetrad

load @term/seed/vibe/hopf
  find hopf
  find axis-of-frame

load @term/seed/vibe/turn
  find rho
  find matrix-of

load @term/seed/atom/flag
  find flag

# THE FRAME OF A SLOT IS THE AXIS OF ITS HOPF CIRCLE: the coordinate pair a slot occupies decides which pair of
# octahedron corners its circle lies over.
rule the-frame-of-a-slot-is-the-axis-of-its-hopf-circle
  seat g, like hurwitz-element
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call q8-axis
        call hurwitz-core
          call hopf
            read g
      call axis-of-frame
        call frame-of
          call unit-slot
            read g
  fold g

# One, as (-1)(-1).
task hurwitz-of-one
  like hurwitz-element
  send back
    call hurwitz-product
      call minus-one-unit
      call minus-one-unit

# THE FULL TURN -1 IS THE OPPOSITE SLOT: the slot of -1 is the opposite of the slot of 1.
rule the-full-turn-is-the-opposite-slot
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call same-tetrad
        call unit-slot
          call minus-one-unit
        call opposite
          call unit-slot
            call hurwitz-of-one
      make yes
  calm hold

# AND THE MATRIX -I OF THE GRID: rho(-1) = -I, the central element of SL(2, 3), which acts on the role grid as the
# point reflection u -> -u.
rule the-full-turn-is-minus-the-identity-on-the-grid
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call rho
        call minus-one-unit
      call matrix-of
        make fear
        make calm
        make calm
        make fear
  calm hold
